# .clinerules — AIML-Project (Exoplanet_Detection)

> Machine-readable + human context for AI coding agents (Cline, etc.).
> Read this FIRST before touching code. Keep it in sync with
> IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md and PROJECT_CONTEXT.md as phases complete.

## 1. What this project is

**AIML-Project / AIML_Exoplanet** — a multi-sector NASA TESS exoplanet
detection pipeline with a false-positive "recycler". It ingests TESS
photometric light curves, detects periodic transit signals with the
Box Least Squares (BLS) algorithm, extracts physics-informed features,
and classifies each target into one of four triage classes, then routes
false positives to specialized diagnostic modules.

**New remote (this repo):** `https://github.com/Dkhatke/AIML-Project.git`
**Old remote (deprecated):** `mahi-mahalle/Exoplanet_Detection.git`

## 2. The four (+1) output classes

```
PLANET    -> sub-stellar occulter (planet candidate)
EB        -> Eclipsing Binary (odd/even depth mismatch, secondary eclipse, V-shape)
VARIABLE  -> stellar pulsation / rotational modulation (sinusoidal/quasi-periodic)
NOISE     -> no significant periodic signal (instrumental or statistical scatter)
REVIEW    -> classifier uncertainty too high (max prob < 0.60); needs human check
```

## 3. Pipeline workflow (module map)

```
TIC ID / star name
  -> src/ingestion/fetcher.py         download_sectors()  multi-sector SPOC->QLP, Parquet cache
  -> src/ingestion/stitcher.py        stitch_sectors()    per-sector normalize + stitch
  -> src/preprocessing/preprocessor.py detrend_lc()       transit-masked two-pass detrend (Wotan)
  -> src/detection/detector.py        run_bls()           frequency-linear bounded BLS + harmonic check
  -> src/features/feature_extractor.py extract_features() 25 ephemeris-blind features (no catalog leakage)
  -> src/classifier/xgb_classifier.py train()/predict_single()  4-class XGBoost + REVIEW threshold
  -> src/recycler/                    route_to_recycler() per-class diagnostics (planet/eb/variable/noise)
```

### Legacy pipeline (still present, being phased out)
`src/fetcher.py`, `src/preprocessor.py`, `src/detector.py`,
`src/analyzer.py`, `src/ml_model.py` — the original single-star HD 209458
demo that still drives the CURRENT `app.py`. Do NOT extend these; new
work goes in the modular `src/<phase>/` packages above. `app.py` is
scheduled for a Phase 6 rewrite onto the modular pipeline.

